  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_037: scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) achieves 0.706 accuracy. The only prior evidence on aggregation (config_002 vs config_003) showed avgpool > transformer by ~7 points, but that was with the weaker pca_n2000 encoder. With the stronger scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l combination, it is unclear whether transformer aggregation could close or reverse that gap. Config_039 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) is a single-variable change from the current best, directly testing whether aggregation strategy matters under the strongest encoder pair. If transformer underperforms, we can confidently lock in avgpool and redirect budget to other axes; if it matches or exceeds avgpool, it opens a new optimization direction. Under a limited budget, resolving this uncertainty with the best-known encoders is more informative than testing a lower-priority axis (e.g., scgpt, which already showed a ~15-point deficit)."
